# Cocos Creator — regenerable state. Covers both the 3.x and 2.x project layouts.
# Every entry below is rebuilt by the editor from `assets/` plus the `.meta` files.
# Comments must be on their own line: a trailing comment after a pattern is matched
# literally and silently ignores nothing.

/library/
/temp/
/local/
/build/

# 3.x only: machine-local editor profiles. 2.x keeps the same kind of state in
# /local/, which is already covered above. Harmless in a 2.x project.
/profiles/

# Native (Android/iOS) build output inside a native project
/native/**/build/
/native/**/.gradle/
/native/**/.cxx/
/native/**/.externalNativeBuild/
/native/**/local.properties

# Editor extensions are committed; their installed dependencies are not.
# 3.x loads them from extensions/, 2.x from packages/.
extensions/*/node_modules/
packages/*/node_modules/

# Staging directory the dev-tools extension renames a cleared cache into before
# deleting it in the background. Never authored, sometimes left behind when the
# editor is closed mid-delete.
/.dev-tools-trash/

# Node tooling
node_modules/
*.log

# These are AUTHORED and must stay tracked. The negations are listed for the same
# reason the ignores are: each one has cost a project real, silent damage.
#
# *.meta          - holds the asset uuid. A missing .meta makes Cocos mint a new uuid,
#                   which breaks every scene and prefab reference without an error.
# /settings/      - shared project configuration (start scene, bundle/build config).
# /build-templates/ - source injected into builds; not the same as /build/. 3.x only.
# /packages/      - in a 2.x project these are the project's own editor extensions,
#                   which ARE authored. Only their node_modules are ignored above.
# package-lock.json - pinned tooling, intentionally committed.
!*.meta
!/settings/
!/build-templates/
!/packages/
!package-lock.json
